  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Faced with Bai Ning Bing’s ice blade storm, Yan Tu answers killer move with killer move. He floods the stage with fuel oil Gu, recalls his two Fiery Snake Gu, and turns the grassland into a sea of fire that the snakes then ride.",
      "chapters": [
        314
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_bai_ning_bing",
        "char_yan_tu",
        "sys_killer_moves",
        "gu_fuel_oil_gu",
        "gu_fiery_snake_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Yan Tu sends all four of his Fiery Claw Gu into the snakes. The snakes grow claws and become fiery dragons. Spectators say he has combined fiery snake Gu and fiery claw Gu to show a portion of rank five fiery dragon Gu might, and they name the killer move fire sea twin dragon kill. The dragons coil around the ice storm, retreat into the inferno to recover, then attack again while the burning grassland replenishes them.",
      "chapters": [
        314
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "composition",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "gu_fiery_claw_gu",
        "sys_killer_moves"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On the same battle stage, fighters treat Fire Sea Twin Dragon Kill as the rare long range method strong enough to stop Ju Kai Bei’s Djinn Transformation assault.",
